WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:14.206
Unit eleven: Weather & Seasons. Today you will describe the weather happening now.

4
00:00:14.506 --> 00:00:17.124
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.427
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.296
Humidity.

7
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:26.956
Humidity means the amount of water in the air.

8
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.259
The humidity makes me sweat.

9
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.479
Your turn. Say: Humidity.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.369
Humidity.

11
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:38.222
Monsoon.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:42.099
Monsoon means the rainy season with strong winds.

13
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.311
The monsoon starts in May.

14
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:47.871
Your turn. Say: Monsoon.

15
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:51.839
Monsoon.

16
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:53.608
Thunderstorm.

17
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:57.336
Thunderstorm means a storm with thunder and lightning.

18
00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.845
A thunderstorm is coming tonight.

19
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.951
Your turn. Say: Thunderstorm.

20
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.743
Thunderstorm.

21
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.299
Drizzle.

22
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:12.049
Drizzle means light rain with very small drops.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.035
It's only a drizzle. Let's go.

24
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.954
Your turn. Say: Drizzle.

25
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.615
Drizzle.

26
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.467
Forecast.

27
00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:27.005
Forecast means a report about the weather to come.

28
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:29.628
The forecast says it will rain.

29
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:32.834
Your turn. Say: Forecast.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.689
Forecast.

31
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.439
Sweltering.

32
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.262
Sweltering means very hot and uncomfortable.

33
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.024
April is sweltering in Cambodia.

34
00:01:45.617 --> 00:01:48.257
Your turn. Say: Sweltering.

35
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.078
Sweltering.

36
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:53.713
Chilly.

37
00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:56.414
Chilly means a little cold.

38
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:58.772
December mornings are chilly.

39
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:01.641
Your turn. Say: Chilly.

40
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.211
Chilly.

41
00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:06.754
Breezy.

42
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.098
Breezy means with a light, pleasant wind.

43
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:12.323
It's breezy by the river.

44
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:15.070
Your turn. Say: Breezy.

45
00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:18.795
Breezy.

46
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.888
Overcast.

47
00:02:21.883 --> 00:02:24.521
Overcast means covered with grey clouds.

48
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.012
The sky is overcast today.

49
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:30.420
Your turn. Say: Overcast.

50
00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.488
Overcast.

51
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.263
Seasonal.

52
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.480
Seasonal means happening only at a certain time of year.

53
00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:42.897
Durian is a seasonal fruit.

54
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:45.869
Your turn. Say: Seasonal.

55
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:49.433
Seasonal.

56
00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:51.138
Downpour.

57
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.962
Downpour means a lot of heavy rain in a short time.

58
00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.190
We got wet in the downpour.

59
00:02:57.783 --> 00:03:00.250
Your turn. Say: Downpour.

60
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.136
Downpour.

61
00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:05.780
Climate.

62
00:03:06.783 --> 00:03:09.212
Climate means the usual weather of a place.

63
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:11.967
Cambodia has a tropical climate.

64
00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:15.294
Your turn. Say: Climate.

65
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.053
Climate.

66
00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:23.657
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:27.401
Visal, look outside! What's happening?

68
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:32.156
It's raining heavily. The wind is blowing hard.

69
00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.669
Is it a thunderstorm?

70
00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:38.331
Yes! The thunder is getting louder.

71
00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:41.242
What does the forecast say?

72
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:46.474
It says the downpour is stopping soon, but it's staying overcast.

73
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:49.192
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:53.129
Grammar focus: Present continuous for now.

75
00:03:53.429 --> 00:03:54.663
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.665
It is raining now.

77
00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.120
The wind is blowing hard.

78
00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:02.063
People are running inside at the moment.

79
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.602
Use the present continuous for things happening right now, as you speak.

80
00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.329
Be careful! Don't say: Look! It rains now.

81
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.768
Say: Look! It is raining now.

82
00:04:16.068 --> 00:04:19.739
For actions happening now, use am, is or are plus -ing.

83
00:04:20.533 --> 00:04:23.128
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:25.561
A Monsoon Afternoon.

85
00:04:25.861 --> 00:04:29.045
Cambodia has a tropical climate with two main seasons.

86
00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:32.335
It has been sweltering and humid all week.

87
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:36.761
Right now, the sky is overcast, and a thunderstorm is coming.

88
00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:40.405
The wind is blowing, and people are running inside.

89
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:46.116
The forecast says the downpour will stop tonight, and tomorrow will be breezy.

90
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.062
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:51.917 --> 00:04:53.721
Look! It blank raining.

92
00:04:54.021 --> 00:04:56.897
A, is. B, are. C, be.

93
00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.328
The answer is A: is.

94
00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:05.669
A report about the weather to come is a blank.

95
00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:09.471
A, forecast. B, climate. C, monsoon.

96
00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.010
The answer is A: forecast.

97
00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.672
Very hot and uncomfortable is blank.

98
00:05:18.972 --> 00:05:22.416
A, sweltering. B, chilly. C, breezy.

99
00:05:25.967 --> 00:05:27.722
The answer is A: sweltering.

100
00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:32.155
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:33.017 --> 00:05:35.724
What is the weather usually like in your favorite season?

102
00:05:44.517 --> 00:05:45.959
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:54.600
My favorite season is the cool season. It's usually breezy and a little chilly in the morning, and it rarely rains.

104
00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.621
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:57.517 --> 00:06:02.038
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present continuous for now.

106
00:06:02.338 --> 00:06:05.977
Today's value is being prepared. Get ready before you go.

107
00:06:06.277 --> 00:06:08.698
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:06:08.998 --> 00:06:11.592
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

